**CONFIRMED regression (blocking): duplicate delivery of a normal final chunk is double-appended.**

On a monotonic stream the terminal chunk arrives with the highest index N while `MaxResponsesChunkIndex == N-1`, so `chunk.ChunkIndex <= accumulator.MaxResponsesChunkIndex` is **false** on the first delivery and `TerminalResponseChunkIndex` is never seeded. When a second plugin delivers the same terminal chunk (logging and maxim both call `tracer.ProcessStreamingChunk` with the same final result: `plugins/logging/main.go:1082`, `plugins/maxim/main.go:587`), the condition `N <= N` is now true, `TerminalResponseChunkIndex` is still -1, so the else branch mints N+1 and the terminal chunk is stored a **second** time. Its `RawResponse` is then written twice into the persisted raw log (`responses.go:907-913`). Before this PR the seen-set deduped that second delivery.

Fix: reserve the terminal index **unconditionally** on the first `isFinalChunk` (exactly like the error path at `responses.go:948-957`), and only remap when it collides:

```go
if isFinalChunk && chunk.StreamResponse != nil {
	if accumulator.TerminalResponseChunkIndex >= 0 {
		chunk.ChunkIndex = accumulator.TerminalResponseChunkIndex
	} else {
		if chunk.ChunkIndex <= accumulator.MaxResponsesChunkIndex {
			accumulator.MaxResponsesChunkIndex++
			chunk.ChunkIndex = accumulator.MaxResponsesChunkIndex
		}
		accumulator.TerminalResponseChunkIndex = chunk.ChunkIndex
	}
}
```

Please also add a test for the monotonic case (terminal chunk has the highest index, delivered twice); the current test only covers the colliding-index case.

